# No Premature Abstraction

Prefer explicit, concrete code over generic frameworks. Abstractions are debt until proven otherwise.

## Hard rules

- **No interface for a single implementation.** An interface is justified only by 2+ real implementations existing today, or a genuine seam (platform backends, test double for external I/O).
- **Do not create** `Manager`, `Service`, `Provider`, `Factory`, `Registry`, `Facade`, `Adapter`, or `Strategy` classes unless explicitly requested. Name classes after what they do (`CardDealer`, `WaveSpawner`), not their pattern.
- **No dependency injection frameworks.** No containers, no `[Inject]`. Wire dependencies with serialized fields, constructor parameters, or direct references.
- **Favor direct references over service locators.** `_audio.Play(clip)` via a serialized/constructor ref beats `Services.Get<IAudioService>().Play(clip)`.
- **Inheritance max 1 level deep** below the framework base class (`MonoBehaviour → Enemy → FlyingEnemy` is the limit). Prefer composition or an enum + switch.
- **Do not abstract until 3 real usages exist.** Two similar blocks of code are allowed to stay similar.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — interface + factory + injection for one implementation
public interface IScoreCalculator { int Calculate(RoundData d); }
public class ScoreCalculatorFactory { public IScoreCalculator Create() => new DefaultScoreCalculator(); }

// ✅ GOOD — a method where the logic is used
private int CalculateScore(RoundData d)
{
    return d.BaseScore * d.Multiplier;
}
```

## Duplication is acceptable

Small duplication is preferred over premature abstraction. Do not unify two code paths behind generics/inheritance if the unified version is harder to read than the two concrete versions. Abstract only when a pattern is **proven** (3+ sites) and the abstraction is simpler than the duplication.

## When an abstraction IS justified

- 2+ real implementations shipped or concretely scheduled (not hypothetical).
- Isolating external I/O (network, storage) for testing.
- A platform seam (editor vs WebGL behavior).

When you introduce one, say why in one sentence in the change description.

## Agent checklist

- [ ] No new interfaces with a single implementation
- [ ] No new *Manager/*Service/*Provider/*Factory/*Registry/*Facade/*Strategy classes unless requested
- [ ] No DI containers or service locators; direct references used
- [ ] Inheritance depth ≤ 1 below framework base
- [ ] Any new abstraction has 3+ usages or an explicit justification
